<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $9.1 bln in July 7 week.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $9.1 bln in July 7 week.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $9.1 billion in the July 7 week to $3,935.8 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $21.5 billion to $5,139.4 billion. M-1 was down $2.6 billion to $1,065.9 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,925.0 billion versus $3,919.4 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
